BT 1 0 0 1 6 508 Tm /F4 7.2 Tf 9.2 TL (- Dependencies and installation steps) Tj T* (- Potential issues and mitigation strategies) Tj T* (- Testing strategy) Tj T*  T* (Structure the plan as a Markdown document with:) Tj T* (1. Overview/Summary) Tj T* (2. File Structure) Tj T* (3. Detailed Implementation Steps \(with checkboxes\)) Tj T* (4. Dependencies & Prerequisites) Tj T* (5. Potential Issues & Mitigations) Tj T* (6. Testing Strategy) Tj T* (7. Success Criteria) Tj T* (8. Next Steps) Tj T*  T* (In the plan, include:) Tj T* (- Estimated time for implementation) Tj T* (- Complexity rating \(1-10\)) Tj T* (- Prerequisites checklist) Tj T* (- Rollback strategy) Tj T*  T* (For enterprise projects, include:) Tj T* (- Security considerations) Tj T* (- Compliance requirements) Tj T* (- Audit logging needs) Tj T* (- Access control review) Tj T*  T* (When planning, consider:) Tj T* (- Development environment) Tj T* (- Staging environment) Tj T* (- Production environment) Tj T* (- Environment-specific variables) Tj T*  T* (### PHASE 4: REVIEW) Tj T* (Ask me to review the plan and provide feedback.) Tj T*  T* (### PHASE 5: IMPLEMENTATION) Tj T* (Only after I approve the plan, generate:) Tj T* (- Complete, production-ready code for all files) Tj T* (- Configuration files) Tj T* (- Documentation) Tj T* (- Deployment instructions) Tj T* (DO NOT implement anything until the plan is approved.) Tj T*  T* (---) Tj T* (### MY REQUEST) Tj T* ([Describe your use case here]) Tj T*  T* (During PLAN MODE:) Tj T* (1. Focus on strategy and design, not implementation details) Tj T* (2. Ask specific, technical questions) Tj T* (3. Reference existing code patterns when relevant) Tj T* (4. Identify potential problems before they occur) Tj T* (5. Provide clear reasoning for each decision) Tj T* (6. Wait for approval before writing any code) Tj T*  T* (Let's begin with PHASE 1: CLARIFICATION.) Tj T* ET
